  "notes": "Five variants. Four are generated by xdrcheck-corpus gen from scenarios/s06-stellar-asset-contract.yaml on a local stellar-core (step sac-trust), at Protocols 28 and 30 on the testnet and public passphrases; they replace the research-probe ledgers this entry first held (evidence/local-core/ and evidence/wallet-backend-731/ keep those runs). The fifth is stellar-core's own golden ledger on the core test passphrase, whose whole-ledger counts equal the local runs', so it shares the expect block: accounts are named through derived.accounts (the scenario's actors are called owner and issuer to match) and the asset through its contract, derived.contracts.sac_usdc, which is the same asset under each variant's passphrase (the golden's asset is IDR). Fee movements are not listed: they are ambient, and the golden's fee bid differs. The wallet-backend#731 acceptance check uses the Protocol 28 variants, because the pre-fix and fixed wallet-backend commits use a Go SDK that cannot decode Protocol 30 ledgers. The Soroban resources in the envelope are declared by the scenario, not simulated (the step runs at Protocol 28); the refund in the fee events reflects that.",
